From: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Subject: mm/mempolicy: compare interleave node size in pages
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 11:28:00 -0800

numa_policy_init() converts node_present_pages() to bytes in an
unsigned long before checking the 16 MiB minimum for init's interleave
nodemask. On a 32-bit NUMA kernel, a node with 4 GiB of present memory
can wrap to zero and be omitted. Processes that inherit init's policy
then fail to interleave allocations across that node.

Compare the page count with the threshold expressed in pages so the
conversion cannot wrap.

Fixes: b71636e29823 ("numa: mempolicy: dynamic interleave map for system init")
Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Cc: David Hildenbrand <david@kernel.org>
Cc: Gregory Price <gourry@gourry.net>
Cc: Zi Yan <ziy@nvidia.com>
Cc: Joshua Hahn <joshua.hahnjy@gmail.com>
Cc: Rakie Kim <rakie.kim@sk.com>
Cc: Ying Huang <ying.huang@linux.alibaba.com>

 mm/mempolicy.c |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/mm/mempolicy.c~mm-mempolicy-compare-interleave-node-size-in-pages
+++ a/mm/mempolicy.c
@@ -3412,7 +3412,7 @@ void __init numa_policy_init(void)
 		}
 
 		/* Interleave this node? */
-		if ((total_pages << PAGE_SHIFT) >= (16 << 20))
+		if (total_pages >= ((16 << 20) >> PAGE_SHIFT))
 			node_set(nid, interleave_nodes);
 	}
 
